@startuml CAP_Host_API
!theme plain

title CAP Protocol - Host API (Reverse Direction)

participant "Host" as H
participant "Plugin Server" as S

note over H, S
  The Host API allows the server to send
  requests **to** the host. This is the
  reverse of normal message flow.
end note

== Create Child Node ==
note over S : Shell plugin wants to create\nartifact node for test output

S -> H : host/create_node\n  node_type: "artifact"\n  args: ["test output"]\n  parent_id: "shell_a1b2c3d4"
activate H
H -> H : Create ArtifactNode\nin context graph
H -> H : Link to parent node
H --> S : { node_id: "artifact_x9y8z7w6" }
deactivate H

== Invoke Method on Host Node ==
note over S : Plugin updates content\non an existing host node

S -> H : host/invoke\n  node_id: "text_m1n2o3p4"\n  method: "set_content"\n  args: ["Updated content"]
activate H
H -> H : Execute method\non target node
H --> S : { result: null }
deactivate H

== Query Filesystem Roots ==
note over S : Plugin discovers\navailable filesystem paths

S -> H : host/query_roots
activate H
H --> S : { roots: [\n  {uri: "file:///project", name: "cwd"},\n  {uri: "file:///home", name: "home"}\n]}
deactivate H

== Resolve Path Through Root ==
note over S : Plugin resolves a\nnormalized path to real path

S -> H : host/resolve_root\n  root_uri: "file:///project"\n  normalized_path: "src/main.py"
activate H
H -> H : Validate root\nResolve path
H --> S : { real_path: "/project/src/main.py",\n  exists: true }
deactivate H

note over H, S
  All Host API requests are gated by host capabilities
  declared during initialize. If capability is false,
  server MUST NOT send the corresponding request.
end note

@enduml
